    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d533">

                <pb facs="0583" n="569" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg569"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.852/92</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-01-18">January 18, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Brazilian Ambassador<anchor n="61" xml:id="d533-f1"/> called at his request.
                    He made a very earnest plea for further consideration by the Navy of the
                    application of his Government presented to Ambassador Caffery and other
                    officials in the State Department for two or three light cruisers to patrol the
                    South Atlantic. I explained to him that the Navy had seemingly failed to act
                    favorably because of an utter lack of vessels which were needed for more urgent
                    services elsewhere. I also made a similar explanation about the request of the
                    Brazilian Government for additional merchant vessels.<anchor n="62"
                        xml:id="d533-f2"/> I said it would give me special satisfaction to urge the
                    appropriate officials in the Government to review and reconsider further these
                    two applications of the Brazilian Government. He expressed his appreciation.</p>
                <p>I then said that I had kept in close touch with Ambassador Caffery in connection
                    with the entire list of things the Brazilian Government desired from this
                    Government and that I felt that we had made real progress in according favorable
                    action on almost all of them, including material and equipment for a military
                    force for the southern area. The Ambassador agreed as to this.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
